component SigilClaimsVocabulary {
  goal {
    Own *AcceptedVocabulary* for interpreted design claims and the rules for
    accepting returned claims as data.
  }

  constraints {
    AcceptedVocabulary This component alone declares the accepted claim names
    and generation. Laws read every relation in the set; an incomplete set is
    an operational error before request preparation.

    *AtomDiscipline* Returned text is parsed and admitted as bounded data. It is
    never run as an egglog program, and external files cannot widen accepted
    forms.
  }

  cases {
    AcceptedVocabulary A row naming a relation or property outside the
    accepted set is refused under these AcceptedVocabulary rules.
  }

  interface {
    AcceptedVocabulary Publish the accepted relations, boolean properties,
    numeric measures, seven contract roles, and vocabulary generation. Reject
    names outside these sets. Change the generation when an incompatible row
    shape or accepted name changes.

    AtomDiscipline Bound artifact bytes and row count before validation.
    Accept only literal-argument data rows; reject rules, commands, schedules,
    nested expressions, and non-literal arguments. Refuse the whole artifact
    when it contains executable or malformed top-level content.
  }
}
